  <IncidentNarrativeParagraph structure="p">On <AccidentDate>November 28,, 2007</AccidentDate>, at <AccidentTime>1800 UTC</AccidentTime>, a <AircraftMakeModel>Cirrus Design Corporation SR-20</AircraftMakeModel>, <AircraftRegistration>N141CD</AircraftRegistration>, serial number <SerialNumber>1032</SerialNumber>, while on approach for landing at <AccidentLocation>Jaleg, Schleswig-Holsteinschen, Germany</AccidentLocation>, struck power lines and subsequently impacted terrain. The airplane was destroyed and the private pilot, the sole person on board the airplane, was fatally injured. Instrument meteorological conditions prevailed at the time of the accident. The cross-country ferry flight originated in the Netherlands and was en route to <DestinationPoint>Sylt, Germany</DestinationPoint>.</IncidentNarrativeParagraph>
  <ForeignInvestigationNote structure="p">This investigation is under the jurisdiction and control of the German government. Any further information may be obtained from:</ForeignInvestigationNote>
